  "body": "Found by the QA swarm round 2 (#2582), brief q04 (sign plate), CamCraft **v0.25.0** Linux x86_64 release over headless MCP; reproduced by hand on the same build.\n\n## What happens\n\nThe part is a plate 160 x 70 x 15 mm (R8 corners) with a 140 x 50 x 4 mm centred pocket and two Ø6 through holes at X = ±70 (on the pocket wall). A 2D Contour, side **outside**, picked on the outer chain, top = top of model, bottom = bottom of model (Z 0), stepdown 3, 4 tabs, Router up-cut 6 mm, generates with `status: ok`, `warnings: 0` and only this note:\n\n```\ndepth: the ring at (72.067, -37.999) ends at its floor Z 7.061 - the part is solid below it; levels below skipped (6.000, 3.000, 2.000, 0.000)\n```\n\nThe point (72.067, -37.999) is 3 mm outside the plate edge (Y = -35), the tool-centre ring. Nothing of the part is below it. The posted program stops at Z 7.061 (G54 Z-8.939 with the WCS at the stock top), so the plate is never cut free and none of the 4 tabs are made. `verify` says `ok: true` with no findings. With `stock_to_leave: 0.02` the false floor moves by exactly +0.02 (Z 7.081 at (72.067, -38.019)). Same result with `tab_count: 0` and with the bottom outer chain picked.\n\nThe generate also takes 133 s for this one contour (re-run on len, 8 cores; the agent saw 3-6 min, so its MCP calls timed out at 3 min).\n\n## Expected\n\nThe contour cuts every level down to Z 0 and makes the 4 tabs, or names a real reason the levels are skipped as a warning, not an ok status.\n\n## Evidence / repro files\n\n- Project: [q04-vcarve-sign-posted-5ops.camproj](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q04-vcarve-sign/q04-vcarve-sign-posted-5ops.camproj) (operation \"Contour Cutout\"), model [q04-vcarve-sign.step](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q04-vcarve-sign/q04-vcarve-sign.step), posted [q04-vcarve-sign.nc](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q04-vcarve-sign/q04-vcarve-sign.nc) (lines 6751-6824).\n- MCP: `open_project {\"path\": \".../q04-vcarve-sign-posted-5ops.camproj\"}`, `generate {\"name\": \"Contour Cutout\"}` gives the note above.\n- Agent report: [REPORT.md](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q04-vcarve-sign/REPORT.md) problem 8.\n\nHow bad: no gouge, but a wrong program passes as ok: the operator finds an uncut plate (7 mm left) and no tabs.\n\nDone means: the q04 project's \"Contour Cutout\" generates every level to Z 0 with its 4 tabs (pinned by a test on this model or a smaller one with a hole on the pocket wall), and a skipped level that is not truly blocked by the part is never reported as only a note.\n",
